;; Semijoin-filter correctness: the three-relation triangle from the
;; benchmark suite, small enough to verify by hand.  The filter (exists
;; tedge keyed on its second column) prunes redge tuples whose source never
;; appears as a tedge destination -- which must not change the output.
;;
;;   triangles: (1,2,4)            via redge(1,2) sedge(2,4) tedge(4,1,7)
;;              (3,2,5)            via redge(3,2) sedge(2,5) tedge(5,3,9)
;;   near-misses that must stay excluded:
;;     redge(6,2): 6 appears in tedge col-1 (tedge 8 6 1) but sedge(2,8)
;;                 is absent, so the 2-path never reaches 8 -- the filter
;;                 PASSES this tuple and the final join rejects it;
;;     redge(7,2): 7 never appears in tedge col-1 -- the filter PRUNES it
;;                 (and without filters the final join rejects it).

table (redge int int)
table (sedge int int)
table (tedge int int int)
table (tri int int int)

facts
(redge 1 2) (redge 3 2) (redge 6 2) (redge 7 2)
(sedge 2 4) (sedge 2 5)
(tedge 4 1 7) (tedge 5 3 9) (tedge 8 6 1)

rule (redge A B) (sedge B C) (tedge C A W) --> (tri A B C)
